WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
This is what we look like on day one of taking beetroots every day.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.360
This is day 50.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.880
They look like the kind of wellness influencers you see every day on social media.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.580
This is day 77, girl.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.540
But none of them are real.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.400
They are AI-generated and designed to sell health supplements on social media.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.140
The Times reviewed hundreds of these ads to understand how AI video tools are helping

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.040
a loosely regulated industry target American consumers

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.020
and profit off of disinformation about their health.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.860
They're targeting us, people that have health issues.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.620
Pamela Wundru is 71.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.800
She's a retired truck driver with a series of health issues

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.300
related to autoimmune disease.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.940
I've always had the joint problems and the inflammation and the fatigue.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.260
So I basically wanted something that was going to help me with all that.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.340
After seeing Facebook ads touting the health effects of moringa,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.520
she placed an order for a popular online supplement brand called Rosabella.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.820
They're pretty good at advertising this stuff.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.580
I do foraging, so I'm always into the plant stuff.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.520
After months of taking her daily dose, she found out some of her pills were contaminated.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.580
It says urgent recall.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.600
In February, the FDA and CDC announced that Rosabella's moringa supplement

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.620
was making people sick with salmonella.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.320
Wunzhou says she didn't experience any symptoms of salmonella,

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.540
but says her health issues got worse while taking the supplement.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.540
When you already have a health problem before this,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.000
and then you take this and then all of a sudden you got worse.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.860
Was this part of it? I don't know. I can't.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.840
I can't say and I don't know how they could prove it either.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.820
Ambrosia Brands, the company behind Rosabella,

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.240
did not respond to multiple requests for comment.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.460
But over the past three years, the company has had hundreds of complaints with the Better Business Bureau.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.240
In Chinese medicine, we have known exactly how to bring this down for generations.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.640
I mean, I believe in Chinese medicine, and I can see how this would hook people because she looks real.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.480
I have seen others where you can tell it's AI.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.300
To me, this does not look like an AI.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.860
So how can we tell if these ads are AI generated?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.420
From American flags to idyllic suburban backgrounds,

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.960
the imagery is repeated over and over

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.520
and is designed to make the ads seem familiar.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.780
Creators also go to great lengths to make their avatars look credible,

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.940
presenting them as doctors or Eastern medical gurus

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.820
with fake diplomas on the walls of their fake offices.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.000
In some cases, the ads make dangerous health claims,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.440
like this one, claiming an herbal supplement

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.060
helped treat kidney disease better than medication.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:49.600
We gave 100 people with stage 3 kidney disease one bottle of Sculptique and told them to take

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.380
ads like these would be illegal on US television, but on the internet they face little enforcement.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:59.040
Meanwhile, creators around the world are cashing in on AI avatars.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.380
Share a link to an Amazon product and get paid commission.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.260
Women over 40 need to hear this.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.560
The people who figure this out are printing money behind the scenes.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.840
In China, AI advertising has exploded as companies seek a quick and easy way to reach the U.S. market.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:25.040
This Chinese agency has been using AI to sell brands on TikTok shop for the past year.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.080
From supplements to toys to electronics, the ads are tailor-made to look American.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.160
Watch and learn, bro.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:43.620
With 40 employees and hundreds of accounts, the company says it produces around 1,200 AI videos like this per day.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.780
at a cost of about $10 each.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.680
Baby Yi declined to show us any supplement ads,

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.120
saying it would violate her contract with the brands.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.280
But she did acknowledge that health products

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.660
need to be handled with extra caution on TikTok.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:21.800
TikTok says it has been banning accounts that make misleading health claims,

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.800
and Meta says it labels AI-generated content on Facebook and Instagram.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.480
But we shared several examples that were still live on these platforms,

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.320
which the companies later removed.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.300
For now, the technology is moving faster than anyone can keep up with.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.440
Many of these online-only brands are operated by anonymous LLCs,

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.620
And there's no federal law limiting the use of synthetic people in advertising.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.500
Meanwhile, these fake wellness influencers are multiplying across our social feeds,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.000
taking advantage of people who can no longer tell what's real.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.440
You want real truth in advertising.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.880
You don't want this fake person.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.160
Anybody could be scammed.
